e92300b7-fd5b-49c2-8708-c9e7ed94e927	pubmed:41817044	pubmed	Machine Learning-Based Risk Prediction Models for Pregnancy-Related Syndromes.	{"Yanqi Wu"}	Pregnancy-related syndromes, such as hypertensive disorders, gestational diabetes mellitus, and preterm birth, pose a significant global health burden, affecting maternal and fetal outcomes. Traditional screening methods, reliant on isolated biomarkers or linear models, often fail to address the complex pathophysiology of these conditions.	2026-03-01	\N	0	Birth defects research	[0.010073553770780563, -0.02141525223851204, -0.004941820167005062, -0.01457430049777031, -0.016076570376753807, 0.007593641057610512, 0.00020892696920782328, 0.07409685105085373, 0.004521990194916725, -0.018343627452850342, 0.00025173358153551817, -0.006956401281058788, -0.020825380459427834, -0.013784659095108509, -0.0032529872842133045, -0.006506933830678463, 0.009884867817163467, -0.005335327237844467, 0.014177507720887661, -0.013932987116277218, 0.0062790666706860065, 0.011541629210114479, 0.010179372504353523, -0.032605089247226715, 0.05279122292995453, 0.017915967851877213, 0.015948981046676636, -0.012447631917893887, -0.03441689908504486, -0.03400978818535805, 0.01844211108982563, -0.04061353951692581, -0.017565416172146797, -0.057789403945207596, 0.02125290408730507, -0.028393885120749474, -0.004809156060218811, -0.011824563145637512, -0.03790730983018875, 0.03844427689909935, -0.0374552458524704, 0.009598083794116974, 0.0105047095566988, -0.005638590082526207, 0.02530563622713089, -0.012380391359329224, 0.025840142741799355, 0.015473333187401295, -0.0025119679048657417, -0.03275846317410469, 0.005723957903683186, 0.007656348403543234, -0.010260790586471558, 0.036539748311042786, 0.04649825021624565, 0.019923193380236626, -0.03182992339134216, -0.0020489145535975695, 0.0129538644105196, 0.029277436435222626, -0.01600472629070282, -0.0035990735050290823, -0.02231232263147831, -0.030936097726225853, -0.01204529870301485, -0.000272471545