8d9cd319-0f78-4b44-8c66-01dfc1d02375	pubmed:41833551	pubmed	Recent advances in synthetic virtual 3D endoscopy to assist in skull base surgery.	{"Victor E Staartjes","Olivier Zanier","Kenneth Arockia","Stefanos Voglis","Giovanni Muscas","Andrea Boschi","Alessandro Della Puppa","Adrian Elmi-Terander","Luca Regli","Carlo Serra"}	The advent of the operating microscope revolutionized neurosurgery by introducing stereoscopic visualization and enabling microneurosurgery. Endoscopy, in turn, brought a compact, wide-angle view through minimal access corridors but sacrificed depth perception. Although 3D endoscopes partially restore stereopsis, they remain costly and hardware dependent. Synthetic or virtual 3D endoscopy aims to recreate depth perception algorithmically from standard 2D endoscopic footage using computer vision and deep learning.	2026-03-15	\N	0	Expert review of neurotherapeutics	[0.006247637327760458, -0.010439373552799225, 0.011695517227053642, 0.005826168227940798, 0.011673101224005222, -0.03017803654074669, 0.012069393880665302, 0.03312646225094795, -0.013544786721467972, -0.03534240648150444, 0.03419031575322151, -0.012943434529006481, -0.008646114729344845, -0.019050633534789085, -0.044410619884729385, -0.0022350021172314882, 0.014755264855921268, -0.003554963506758213, 0.007527698762714863, -0.021152546629309654, 0.010271415114402771, 0.02212129533290863, -0.011785189621150494, -0.024991458281874657, 0.031236078590154648, -0.0030866956803947687, 0.040479205548763275, 0.00718015618622303, -0.021321553736925125, -0.07126732170581818, 0.020435061305761337, -0.018374085426330566, 0.01778700016438961, -0.01968325488269329, 0.016473252326250076, -0.004965537693351507, 0.02169201150536537, -0.008707105182111263, -0.03679414838552475, 0.01853249780833721, -0.03360744193196297, 0.00740781519562006, 0.002488059224560857, -0.02130170725286007, -0.01135065034031868, -0.006959327030926943, 0.008185287937521935, 0.020745256915688515, 0.02745267190039158, -0.0077104680