d22e84af-15b3-4338-bb00-43badb398404	pubmed:41875245	pubmed	A Bilingual Arabic-English Ambient AI Scribe for Clinical Documentation: Prospective Evaluation Study.	{"Umair Tahir Khan","Ammar Tahir Khan","Waleed Aljaadi","Razan Alhadlaq","Zahran Baqashmer","Yasin Alsafi","Yousef Alomran","Maha Al Rusaiyes","Muaddiyah Radif","Tahir Naeem Khan","Saleh Abdullah Saleh Altamimi"}	Medical ambient artificial intelligence (AI) scribes reduce documentation burden, but the current evidence is almost entirely from English systems. In the Arabic-speaking world, physicians converse mainly in Arabic and write clinical notes in English, adding cognitive burden. Due to scarce corpora in the Arabic language, the development of Arabic-enabled AI speech technologies has been challenging. Here, we address this gap by developing and evaluating a bilingual Arabic-English medical AI scribe.	2026-03-24	\N	0	JMIR medical informatics	[0.02675142139196396, -0.02382911555469036, 0.008862019516527653, -0.004842940717935562, -0.013524599373340607, -0.03073638677597046, 0.015141353942453861, 0.04588763788342476, -0.031126759946346283, -0.0009132649865932763, 0.043973106890916824, -0.04879332333803177, -0.008389294147491455, 0.00818090233951807, -0.01872969977557659, -0.016160698607563972, 0.05957508459687233, 0.027250181883573532, -0.021466247737407684, -0.028044292703270912, -0.011535092256963253, 0.005024998914450407, 0.012214436195790768, -0.01433625165373087, 0.06770613044500351, -0.022847680374979973, 0.018740860745310783, -0.0028833772521466017, -0.00024972669780254364, -0.03724107891321182, -0.01443496160209179, -0.012408258393406868, 0.008453862741589546, -0.03887751325964928, 0.004134314134716988, -0.005639407783746719, 0.005300266668200493, -0.027368180453777313, -0.02517593838274479, 0.02051999792456627, -0.02586229145526886, -0.0022507947869598866, 0.0062885466031730175, -0.025178631767630577, -0.006074075121432543, 0.02324613928794861, 0.04232347384095192, 0.016986453905701637, -0.0165