c49f1815-84d3-45d5-ac07-62932a5e3071	pubmed:41875437	pubmed	An echo from the past: open access repository of over 10,000 annotated Doppler audio recordings of venous gas emboli.	{"S Lesley Blogg","Arian Azarang","Rachel Lance","Frauke Tillmans","Richard Moon","Virginie Papadopoulou","Peter Lindholm"}	Doppler ultrasound measurements have been recorded since the 1970s across the world and provide a valuable data resource for learning, analysis, and potential training of deep learning algorithms to recognise and grade venous gas emboli (VGE) allowing assessment of decompression sickness (DCS) risk.	2026-03-31	\N	0	Diving and hyperbaric medicine	[0.023577764630317688, 0.008240058086812496, 0.013328822329640388, 0.029826635494828224, -0.02091890014708042, -0.013162055052816868, 0.025856858119368553, 0.051993995904922485, -0.006127955857664347, -0.013845663517713547, 0.0499412976205349, -0.004092067945748568, 0.00515585346147418, 0.017740685492753983, -0.03632520139217377, -0.024836748838424683, -0.0007680402486585081, -0.009197506122291088, 0.015297971665859222, -0.0063259233720600605, 0.025223607197403908, -0.0009355731308460236, -0.0027484174352139235, -0.03767336905002594, 0.013781980611383915, 0.011465409770607948, 0.00485428748652339, 0.019839897751808167, -0.015569604933261871, -0.02758079580962658, -0.00041010958375409245, -0.012248390354216099, -0.0033188951201736927, -0.023873720318078995, 0.00011661622556857765, -0.020087119191884995, 0.030259760096669197, -0.01714143715798855, -0.025364138185977936, 0.011995323933660984, -0.003776454133912921, 0.018603933975100517, -0.005808161571621895, -0.01692623645067215, 0.01601583883166313, -0.017562324181199074, 0.015084008686244488, 0.04552460089325905, 0.003388740587979555, -0.020443834364414215, 0.02561257779598236, 0.019953198730945587, 0.02718314528465271, -0.003068524179980159, 0.011600658297538757, 0.011168133467435837, -0.014288229867815971, -0.020682131871581078, -0.031531620770692825, 0.009133497253060341, -0.