d57feb2b-5283-43e8-8b91-b29d7e4f22f2	pubmed:41875224	pubmed	Comparison of Large Language Models with Rules-Based Natural Language Processing Algorithms for Extracting Data from Operative Notes.	{"Linjun Yang","Kellen L Mulford","Miguel M Girod-Hoffman","Monty Khela","Amirali Khosravi","Derek M Crossman","Anish Kanabar","Sami Saniei","Marisa N Ulrich","Michael J Taunton","Cody C Wyles"}	We aimed to develop automated data extraction pipelines with large language models (LLMs) to extract registry data from total hip arthroplasty (THA) operative notes and compare the performance with that of existing natural language processing (NLP) algorithms.	2026-03-24	\N	0	The Journal of bone and joint surgery. American volume	[0.006224131677299738, -0.01693747378885746, 0.020915772765874863, -0.004526369273662567, -0.013663538731634617, 0.0030740131624042988, 0.003443218069151044, 0.09065733104944229, -0.05112963914871216, -0.013971234671771526, 0.03492414951324463, -0.016497714444994926, -0.02434651367366314, 0.0008296995656564832, -0.02684824727475643, -3.707202631630935e-05, 0.011715843342244625, 0.02476043999195099, 0.011211114935576916, -0.004069096874445677, 0.010779542848467827, 0.02252032980322838, -0.005516508128494024, -0.010083765722811222, 0.04749767482280731, -0.031071409583091736, 0.034383535385131836, -0.0009449452045373619, -0.04543308913707733, -0.04628560319542885, 0.009630449116230011, -0.004160878248512745, 0.0015154511202126741, -0.016437716782093048, 0.011388089507818222, 0.008105406537652016, 0.016620401293039322, 0.000815784907899797, -0.04438688978552818, 0.03316650167107582, -0.022067870944738388, 0.026426419615745544, 0.0005822962848469615, -0.014020627364516258, 0.03290412575006485, -0.014571121893823147, 0.02576962299644947, 0.011636992916464806, -0.016246506944298744, -0.008674001321196556, 0.009657055139541626, 0.015742095187306404, 0.018748803064227104, 0.04186424985527992, 0.028035784140229225, 0.013171639293432236, -0.030254729092121124, -0.021057