71ec1534-0bde-4693-87ea-433022bf9b73	pubmed:41875247	pubmed	Thrombopoietin receptor agonists in immune thrombocytopenia: a comparative review of mechanisms, efficacy, and the future of personalized management.	{"Emmanuel Andrès","Xavier Jannot","Jean Edouard Terrade","Noel Lorenzo-Villalba"}	Thrombopoietin receptor agonists (TPO-RAs) have reshaped the management of chronic immune thrombocytopenia (ITP) by directly targeting impaired platelet production, a mechanism previously overshadowed by immune-mediated destruction. The three approved agents - romiplostim, eltrombopag, and avatrombopag - all stimulate the c-Mpl receptor but differ in their molecular interactions, pharmacokinetics, and potential immunomodulatory properties.	2026-03-24	\N	0	Expert opinion on pharmacotherapy	[-0.005204508546739817, -0.04734884202480316, -0.011667748913168907, 0.008069800212979317, 0.02054164931178093, -0.017106270417571068, 0.0009660425712354481, 0.07296716421842575, -0.010315620340406895, 0.0002709116961341351, 0.03721200302243233, -0.01689799316227436, -0.016866957768797874, -0.013082328252494335, -0.010816806927323341, -0.02376469224691391, 0.012294027023017406, 0.017578577622771263, 0.010092642158269882, -0.0029721695464104414, -0.003630162449553609, 0.01567717455327511, 0.009701008908450603, -0.02183355577290058, 0.03956269100308418, 0.017296403646469116, 0.0027682329528033733, -0.004526181612163782, -0.034494929015636444, -0.04145302623510361, 0.005147363059222698, 0.005242967512458563, -0.015664203092455864, -0.04274851456284523, 0.021888989955186844, -0.03307799994945526, -0.007915832102298737, -0.006364324130117893, -0.035150833427906036, 0.0042668292298913, -0.03164936974644661, 0.0011431511957198381, 0.007908020168542862, -0.029476210474967957, 0.0014498555101454258, 0.01985185034573078, -0.0009394805529154837, 0.017917362973093987, 0.01869879476726055, -0.011773783713579178, 0.0232760738581419, -0.018138883635401726, -0.01628158800303936, 0.04961498826742172, 0.02625549