eaefdf92-3017-4833-8abe-1fd9557b58e8	arxiv:2603.25723v1	arxiv	Natural-Language Agent Harnesses	{"Linyue Pan","Lexiao Zou","Shuo Guo","Jingchen Ni","Hai-Tao Zheng"}	Agent performance increasingly depends on \\emph{harness engineering}, yet harness design is usually buried in controller code and runtime-specific conventions, making it hard to transfer, compare, and study as a scientific object. We ask whether the high-level control logic of an agent harness can instead be externalized as a portable executable artifact. We introduce \\textbf{Natural-Language Agent Harnesses} (NLAHs), which express harness behavior in editable natural language, and \\textbf{Intelligent Harness Runtime} (IHR), a shared runtime that executes these harnesses through explicit contracts, durable artifacts, and lightweight adapters. Across coding and computer-use benchmarks, we conduct controlled evaluations of operational viability, module ablation, and code-to-text harness migration.	2026-03-26	https://arxiv.org/pdf/2603.25723v1	0	\N	[0.036427874118089676, -0.007697990629822016, -0.021835235878825188, 0.00035896411282010376, -0.013723724521696568, -0.05027250200510025, 0.032852642238140106, 0.05734797939658165, -0.014492231421172619, -0.014092748053371906, 0.029260626062750816, -0.04599544405937195, -0.009321527555584908, -0.010559218935668468, -0.032946955412626266, -0.0029443714302033186, 0.037069663405418396, -0.02097526751458645, 0.008670001290738583, -0.008964459411799908, 0.010876815766096115, 0.006956450641155243, -0.005613268818706274, -0.028436899185180664, 0.04685768857598305, 0.01880585588514805, -0.013926676474511623, -0.005215269513428211, 0.0073180715553462505, -0.003996299579739571, 0.007015478331595659, -0.0011601039441302419, -0.003872669767588377, -0.039712924510240555, 0.016673965379595757, -0.022494040429592133, -0.005224390421062708, -0.03628087788820267, -0.029450776055455208, 0.02608932927250862, -0.024642743170261383, 0.004134580958634615, 0.025789817795157433, -0.04